{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"rg -n \\\"reference_count|reading_report|25|reference|bibliogr\\\" validate_artifacts.py REPRODUCIBILITY.md | tail -24; tail -9 build_claims.py; tail -20 scientific-evidence/schemas/artifact-manifest.schema.json; sed -n '1,30p' .codex/skills/scientific-evidence/scripts/scientific_evidence.sh; ls -la /tmp/repo_support 2>/dev/null; rg -n '75%|bibliography|citation|reference' paper.tex | tail -14; ls -l figures\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"rg -n \\\"reference_count|reading_report|25|reference|bibliogr\\\" validate_artifacts.py REPRODUCIBILITY.md | tail -24; tail -9 build_claims.py; tail -20 scientific-evidence/schemas/artifact-manifest.schema.json; sed -n '1,30p' .codex/skills/scientific-evidence/scripts/scientific_evidence.sh; ls -la /tmp/repo_support 2>/dev/null; rg -n '75%|bibliography|citation|reference' paper.tex | tail -14; ls -l figures\"","aggregated_output":"REPRODUCIBILITY.md:67:Use the staged `validate-paper` scripts for source/citation checks, claim/provenance checks, figure schema/readability checks, compilation and visible Supplementary Information checks. Use the `scientific-evidence` verifier for dangling-reference checks. `validation_report.json` records the performed checks and any environmental limitation; it must not be interpreted as a substitute for a human scientific review. No private-entropy generation, new component ablation or missing gate diagnostic is inferred from a passing artifact check.\nvalidate_artifacts.py:29:for name, arguments in [('tex_references', [sys.executable, CHECKS / 'validate_tex_refs.py', '--tex', 'paper.tex', '--bib', 'references.bib'])]:\nvalidate_artifacts.py:81:from src.orchestrator.paper_step import compute_last_body_page_fill_ratio, find_reference_start_page, find_supplement_start_page, read_pdf_page_layouts, read_pdf_page_texts, validate_visible_language\nvalidate_artifacts.py:84:reference_start = find_reference_start_page(pages)\nvalidate_artifacts.py:86:body_pages = reference_start - 1\nvalidate_artifacts.py:88:                                       reference_start_page=reference_start, body_columns=1)\nvalidate_artifacts.py:90:    'body_pages': body_pages, 'last_body_page_fill_ratio': fill, 'reference_start_page': reference_start,\nvalidate_artifacts.py:101:reference_count = len(json.loads((ROOT / 'references_provenance.json').read_text())['references'])\nvalidate_artifacts.py:102:REPORT['checks']['reference_count'] = reference_count\nvalidate_artifacts.py:103:if not 25 <= reference_count <= 30:\nvalidate_artifacts.py:107:digest = hashlib.sha256()\nvalidate_artifacts.py:118:identity = {'selected_tree_sha256': 'sha256:' + digest.hexdigest(),\nvalidate_artifacts.py:119:            'sealed_tree_sha256': REGISTRY['final_evaluation']['program_tree_sha256'],\nvalidate_artifacts.py:120:            'evaluator_copy_sha256': 'sha256:' + hashlib.sha256((ROOT / 'source_evidence/evaluate_final.py').read_bytes()).hexdigest(),\nvalidate_artifacts.py:121:            'sealed_evaluator_sha256': REGISTRY['final_evaluation']['evaluator_sha256'],\nvalidate_artifacts.py:124:identity['passed'] = identity['selected_tree_sha256'] == identity['sealed_tree_sha256'] and identity['evaluator_copy_sha256'] == identity['sealed_evaluator_sha256'] and identity['selected_source_copy_equal']\nvalidate_artifacts.py:131:    'paper.tex': ['paper_data.json', 'references_provenance.json', 'source_evidence/adaptive.py', 'source_evidence/evaluate_final.py'],\nvalidate_artifacts.py:132:    'paper.pdf': ['paper.tex', 'references.bib', 'figure_manifest.json', 'tables/condition_means.tex'],\nvalidate_artifacts.py:133:    'claims_grounding.json': ['paper.tex', 'paper_data.json', 'references_provenance.json', 'build_claims.py'],\nvalidate_artifacts.py:135:    'references.bib': ['references_provenance.json', 'finalize_references.py'],\nvalidate_artifacts.py:136:    'references_provenance.json': ['literature/reading_report.txt', 'finalize_references.py'],\nvalidate_artifacts.py:144:                     'sha256': hashlib.sha256(artifact.read_bytes()).hexdigest()},\nvalidate_artifacts.py:150:if run('claims', [sys.executable, ROOT / '.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py', '--paper-data', 'paper_data.json', '--references', 'references_provenance.json', '--bib', 'references.bib', '--claims', 'claims_grounding.json', '--paper-dir', '.']).returncode:\nvalidate_artifacts.py:162:if evidence_result.returncode or evidence_report['summary']['dangling_references']:\nclaim('No isolated shrinkage, Hellinger, group-calibration, structural-zero, real-data or full-data-refit evaluation supports broader attribution; shifted conditions alter the sampling law and cannot validate exchangeability-based or conditional claims.', [EPISODES, 'result.top_program_01', 'result.top_program_02', 'result.top_program_03'], ('Tibshirani2019', 'Barber2023', 'Barber2021Limits'), ('source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:776-814',))\ndurations = SUMMARY['duration_seconds']\nclaim(f'Observed retained seed duration totals range from {min(durations):.9f} to {max(durations):.9f} seconds; not end-to-end or hardware-specific reproduction timings.', [EPISODES])\nclaim('The evaluated NumPy requirement is 2.2.6; exact resource recreation is not possible from public seed labels alone because private entropy is used. Replay requires frozen NPZ arrays and manifests. Readable evaluated copies, not hashes alone, support implementation facts.', [EPISODES, 'result.top_program_01'], paths=['source_evidence/requirements.txt', 'source_evidence/manifest.json', 'source_evidence/final_resource_manifest.json', 'source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:768-814'])\n\nclaim('Foundational related-work distinctions: compositional log-ratio representation and logistic-normal modeling; regression split calibration; quantile adaptation; label-set prediction; cross-fitting versus jackknife+; marginal versus conditional validity; shift correction; proper probabilistic scores.', ['ref.' + key for key in ['Aitchison1982','Egozcue2003','AitchisonShen1980','Pawlowsky2011','Vovk2005','Papadopoulos2002','Lei2018','Romano2019','Romano2020','Ding2023','Barber2021Jackknife','Vovk2012','Barber2021Limits','Tibshirani2019','Barber2023','Gneiting2007']], ['Aitchison1982','Egozcue2003','AitchisonShen1980','Pawlowsky2011','Vovk2005','Papadopoulos2002','Lei2018','Romano2019','Romano2020','Ding2023','Barber2021Jackknife','Vovk2012','Barber2021Limits','Tibshirani2019','Barber2023','Gneiting2007'])\n\n(ROOT / 'claims_grounding.json').write_text(json.dumps({'claims': CLAIMS}, indent=2) + '\\n')\nprint(f'Wrote {len(CLAIMS)} grounded claim groups.')\n        ]\n      },\n      \"description\": \"Optional machine-readable outputs emitted by the derivation.\",\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"notes\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"schema_name\": {\n      \"const\": \"scientific-evidence.artifact-manifest\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"schema_name\",\n    \"artifact\",\n    \"derived_from\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"Scientific Evidence Artifact Manifest\",\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\nset -euo pipefail\n\nSCRIPT_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd)\"\nexec python3 \"$SCRIPT_DIR/scientific_evidence.py\" \"$@\"\n123:The principal comparison is between fitted systems rather than training-size-matched geometry interventions. In particular, the reference locations use only three quarters of the training observations, whereas the adaptive location uses all of them after residual cross-fitting. The single-split adaptive comparison also changes residual allocation and location refitting together. We therefore do not infer that any difference is caused solely by cross-fitting, boundary grouping, or covariance adjustment.\n183:The boundary-concentrated Dirichlet condition reverses the favorable efficiency story. Adaptive ILR has volume 0.9759 and coverage 0.8947. The isotropic ILR ball has volume 0.999998, effectively the full simplex at the reported resolution, whereas the Euclidean ball uses 0.7155 with coverage 0.8992. The adaptive shape reduces volume relative to isotropic ILR but does not make the region compact relative to the raw-simplex reference. A near-full-simplex region can achieve unremarkable coverage on a boundary-concentrated response distribution because uniform simplex volume is not response probability mass. This is a limitation of the tested score/geometry combination, not an integration-based proof of good uncertainty quality.\n198:\\caption{Descriptive sign-stratum reliability in heteroskedastic and shifted conditions. Dots show each held-out seed and bars show means. Masks for different covariates overlap; their coverage rates are not simultaneous guarantees. The nominal line is a reference only. No empty-mask zero encodings are plotted.}\n208:The equal-weight six-condition adaptive averages are coverage 0.8942 and volume 0.5446. Aggregate paired contrasts in Table~\\ref{tab:contrasts} favor adaptive ILR over the isotropic ILR reference in both coverage and volume, but not over Euclidean in volume. In particular, the Euclidean volume-reduction interval is entirely negative. This aggregate includes correlated C2-derived controls and the shifted condition, so it is not a population marginal coverage estimate or an estimate over six independent task families. The separate condition results, rather than this summary, establish the paper's central trade-off.\n219:Euclidean & Coverage: adaptive minus reference & $-0.0014$ & $[-0.0065,0.0039]$ \\\\\n220:Euclidean & Volume: reference minus adaptive & $-0.0346$ & $[-0.0546,-0.0115]$ \\\\\n221:ILR ball & Coverage: adaptive minus reference & $0.0251$ & $[0.0185,0.0319]$ \\\\\n222:ILR ball & Volume: reference minus adaptive & $0.0496$ & $[0.0306,0.0618]$ \\\\\n249:Several limitations constrain interpretation. The response families are synthetic, strictly positive, and low-dimensional relative to many applications. No real dataset, structural-zero case, label-set task, alternative score geometry, or weighted shift calibration was evaluated. The boundary and shifted conditions also change response family and dimension relative to the logistic-normal conditions; their comparison is a regime contrast, not an isolated intervention on boundary proximity or shift. The reference fits use fewer training rows than the adaptive location, and the auxiliary residual comparison bundles changes. Neither causal mechanism attribution nor an optimality claim follows.\n266:\\bibliography{references}\n267:\\bibliographystyle{paper}\n467:References were checked by direct identifiers against bibliographic services and official abstract pages, with selected conformal full texts inspected. The supplied broad retrieval was narrowed to foundational sources relevant to the manuscript. Reading scope is recorded per reference; this is not a systematic literature review or a certification of novelty. No task-identifying literature search or citation-chain traversal was used during manuscript preparation. No prohibited-source encounter was identified in this writing step; this statement does not certify unseen earlier activity.\n468:% @evidence[[references_provenance.json]]\n472:LLM agents assisted with research design proposals, implementation editing, reference-query planning, source inspection, framing, manuscript drafting, and construction of plotting and claim-mapping code. Numerical findings in this paper are retained outputs of the executable evaluation, not language-model estimates. During manuscript preparation, code derived tables and figures from those existing outputs; no new model experiment was performed. LLM-assisted evidence checking links claims to source artifacts, but does not replace scientific validation or independent review. No independent human audit is claimed.\ntotal 432\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent  27170 Nov  7 06:42 coverage_volume_by_regime.pdf\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent    531 Nov  7 06:42 coverage_volume_by_regime.pdf.prov.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent 118481 Nov  7 06:42 coverage_volume_by_regime.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent    531 Nov  7 06:42 coverage_volume_by_regime.png.prov.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent  30598 Nov  7 06:42 descriptive_sign_strata.pdf\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent    529 Nov  7 06:42 descriptive_sign_strata.pdf.prov.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent  79053 Nov  7 06:42 descriptive_sign_strata.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent    529 Nov  7 06:42 descriptive_sign_strata.png.prov.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent   8463 Nov  7 06:16 geometry_calibration_overview.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent      3 Nov  7 06:16 geometry_calibration_overview.prompts.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent  21487 Nov  7 06:42 search_configuration_comparison.pdf\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent    504 Nov  7 06:42 search_configuration_comparison.pdf.prov.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent 112169 Nov  7 06:42 search_configuration_comparison.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent    504 Nov  7 06:42 search_configuration_comparison.png.prov.json\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
